{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","version":"2.1.0","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"pmat","informationUri":"https://github.com/paiml/aprender","rules":[]}},"invocations":[{"executionSuccessful":true,"commandLine":"cargo mutants (private CARGO_TARGET_DIR, systemd-run units); git diff 30035481ae..d5992f06d4 read by hand"}],"results":[{"ruleId":"review.mutants-missed-under-ci-lib-shard","level":"error","message":{"text":"Ran cargo-mutants over release_crux.rs, release_evidence.rs and extract/mod.rs with the CI shard shape (--lib, in-diff, timeout 300). Stopped by the reviewer after 96 mutants: 71 caught, 25 MISSED. 20 are in release_crux.rs (Entry::has_counterpart :43, read_mapping :81/:93, entry_of :124, engines_of :136/:137, read_receipts :167/:170/:187, rows_of :199, emit :269-:295), 5 in release_evidence.rs project :508/:525. The tests that would kill the release_crux.rs mutants live in the aprender-contracts-cli crate and ci/mutants-feature-groups.txt has no row for release_crux.rs or release_evidence.rs, so the default --lib shard cannot see them. Commit 4f319869e6 itself states 22 misses. MUTANTS_MAX_MISSED=0 on the PR diff would fail."},"properties":{"grounding":"measured","command":["cargo","mutants","-p","aprender-contracts","--in-diff","pr.diff","--no-times","--timeout","300","-j","5","--file","release_crux.rs","--file","release_evidence.rs","--file","extract/mod.rs","--","--lib"],"exit_code":2,"stdout_sha256":"2f8207aa9a66cffcaa2388b43e683788c2cfee41f7e88faf0a1fdb2ccace3706","failure_scenario":"A regression that makes emit count rows wrongly or read_receipts skip a receipt passes every --lib test in aprender-contracts, so the CI mutants shard goes red on these survivors.","precision_class":"advisory"}},{"ruleId":"review.mutants-timeout-obligations-load","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Under the aprender-contracts-cli obligations.rs row (copy-vcs, timeout 300), mutant obligations.rs:157:16 replace == with != in load (the merge-key fixpoint loop) TIMED OUT rather than being caught: the loop never terminates when doc == before is inverted. Other results for the file: 77 caught, 4 unviable, 1 timeout. Whether the CI gate counts TIMEOUT as killed is not verified."},"properties":{"grounding":"measured","command":["cargo","mutants","-p","aprender-contracts-cli","--file","obligations.rs","--in-diff","pr.diff","--no-times","--timeout","300","--copy-vcs","true","--","--lib"],"exit_code":3,"stdout_sha256":"82aad4813e2525ff6cb246f70b02eefe2fef5af89012a9df22bb45ccfdf17c54","failure_scenario":"If the gate treats TIMEOUT as a survivor the obligations row is red on this one mutant; if as killed, the mutant is stopped by a hang timeout, not by an assertion.","precision_class":"advisory"}},{"ruleId":"review.lint-row-not-measured","level":"warning","message":{"text":"The aprender-contracts-cli lint.rs row could not be measured: cargo-mutants failed the unmutated baseline (Timeout, rc 4) even with --copy-vcs true under host load. Whether the new meet() tests kill their target mutants is not_measured."},"properties":{"grounding":"asserted","rationale":"Baseline timeout on a loaded shared host, not evidence about the tests.","failure_scenario":"meet() mutants such as flipping the armed comparison could survive; no measurement either way.","precision_class":"advisory"}},{"ruleId":"review.batch-b-not-run","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Mutants in challenge.rs and proof_status.rs (find_word reorder tests) and the rest of batch A were not run: the reviewer stopped the units for time. not_measured, so the survivor list is a lower bound."},"properties":{"grounding":"asserted","rationale":"Run stopped by reviewer; nothing was inferred for the unrun mutants.","failure_scenario":"A find_word mutant the reordered asserts fail to kill would not appear here.","precision_class":"advisory"}},{"ruleId":"review.obligations-if-refactor-hides-branch","level":"note","message":{"text":"obligations.rs load: splitting the Parse and Other error arms is behaviour-equivalent but removes an if problems.is_empty() that cargo-mutants would have tested. This looks like shaping code to the mutation tool: a possibly dead branch leaves the mutant universe rather than being proven dead or covered."},"properties":{"grounding":"asserted","rationale":"Read by hand from the diff; equivalence checked for the two arms only.","failure_scenario":"If the branch carried a case unreachable from the two arms, the refactor drops a check; unparseable_yaml_is_one_problem covers the Parse arm only.","precision_class":"advisory"}},{"ruleId":"review.script-and-rows-not-weaker","level":"note","message":{"text":"scripts/mutants_table_shard.sh and check_mutants_feature_groups.sh: an empty feature field is now legal (no --features passed), the args column stays required, timeout 900 unchanged, --in-diff and --shard kept, so no mutant leaves the universe. The five new no-feature cli rows only add mutants. The fake-cargo cases (no-feature-row GREEN, no-feature-survivor RED, row-without-args DEAD) exercise each branch. Gates read as at least as strict."},"properties":{"grounding":"asserted","rationale":"Read the diffs; the check_mutants_feature_groups.sh self-test was not re-run by this reviewer.","failure_scenario":"An empty-features row silently dropping --features for a crate that needs one would build the wrong feature set; the added rows need none.","precision_class":"advisory"}},{"ruleId":"review.no-row-for-release-crux","level":"warning","message":{"text":"ci/mutants-feature-groups.txt covers only aprender-contracts-cli files; no row runs the cli tests against crates/aprender-contracts files (release_crux.rs, release_evidence.rs, extract/mod.rs). Fix direction, not made here: add a package-crossing row or move the tests into aprender-contracts."},"properties":{"grounding":"asserted","rationale":"Read the row list against the diff file list.","failure_scenario":"Changes to those files are mutation-tested only by 